dialogue trust_engineer_3
title: Tap Seven
trigger: Trust engineer level=3
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  A trader's mule left a folded paper at the edge of camp, tied with red wire. The Engineer has read it twice and is now taking apart a perfectly good lantern, very fast.
  * That lantern was working. What's in the paper? -> paper
    do: AddTrust $with 3
  * Bad news travels on red wire, does it? -> wire
    do: AddTrust $with 5
  * Put the lantern back together. We need the light. -> lantern
    do: AddTrust $with -2

node paper hero
  It was working. Now it isn't, and now I know why it was. That's how I calm down. The paper's from home. Read it if you like. It doesn't say much.
  -> redline

node wire hero
  It does if it's Redline sending it. Red wire is how they sign. Nobody else in the Underspire would waste good wire on a letter.
  -> redline

node lantern hero
  I'll put it back. Better than it was. It's how I think, Commander, with my hands in something. The paper's from home, and I'm thinking hard.
  -> redline

node redline hero
  Redline runs the fish market, and the fish market runs on Tap Seven, and Tap Seven ran on me. Every night for six years. Until the night it didn't.
  -> dark

node dark hero
  A seal went. A Halcyon seal, older than the market. The tap shut itself off, and half the lower city went dark for three days, and in the dark people got hurt. Redline decided that was a debt, and the debt was mine.
  -> dig

node dig hero
  That's why I took the Choir's dig job. It paid enough to clear it. Then the Choir paid me in blessings, and you found me in the red with a canteen. And now Redline knows where I am.
  -> demand

node demand commander
  The Engineer holds out the paper. In blunt capitals it names a sum, a place on the Underspire road, and a season. Underneath, smaller: bring the orb and we're square.
  -> ask

node ask commander
  The Engineer stops taking the lantern apart and waits.
  * Your debt is the crew's debt now. When the road goes that way, we pay it together. -> shared
    do: AddTrust $with 9
    do: SetFlag engineer:debt_shared
  * A seal older than the market failed. That's no debt of yours. Redline gets nothing. -> defied
    do: AddTrust $with 7
    do: SetFlag engineer:debt_defied
  * The orb stays with me. If Redline wants you, that's yours to settle. -> sent
    do: AddTrust $with -4
    do: SetFlag engineer:debt_sent

node shared hero
  Together. With a whole crew behind me, Redline can count all it likes. I'm going to need a bigger notebook for what I owe you, though.
  -> close_line

node defied hero
  Nobody's said that to me. Not once in two years. I said it to myself plenty, but it doesn't count when you're the one who held the wrench.
  -> close_line

node sent hero
  Mine to settle. Right. I was hired here too, then. I'd started to forget. I won't hand them the orb, Commander, if that's what you're worried about. I'm not Redline.
  -> close_line

node close_line hero
  The seal. I still think about it. Halcyon parts don't just fail. Something told that tap to shut. I'd like to know what, someday.
  -> close

node close commander
  The lantern goes back together in a dozen quick turns. When the Engineer strikes it, it burns brighter than it did before, and the red-wired paper goes into the fire.
